<p>I got summoned by IRC. Let's crit this.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Here,&nbsp;have&nbsp;some&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;OK,&nbsp;now&nbsp;give&nbsp;me&nbsp;back&nbsp;my&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>At least five millilitres of blood from this nosebleed must drop into the cup for the memory to be stored.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It looks like it would be very difficult to get the blood inside the cup, as most people don't usually put their drink directly under their nose. At this point almost everyone would have permanent retrograde amnesia. Maybe it could be better if the memory gets stolen by having contact with the person's saliva?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>If someone who has already drunk the substance once attempts to swallow it again, it blocks the trachea and cannot be removed by any known means until the drinker dies of asphyxiation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Maybe you could make the second drinkers to have permanent amnesia? If the object revolves around memory, the &quot;punishment&quot; should also be regarding memory.</p>
<p>Regarding the Central Narrative, maybe it would be better if the woman doesn't comMits suicide, but instead comes to Foundation attention and they interrogate her? And in the interview she could say the memory first come to her mind after drinking from the cup.</p>
<p>Regarding the Hook, my concern is that your Hook is about the anomaly's ability to alter memories. There are already many articles about memory affecting anomalies. My advice is to focus on telling a story. Maybe you can focus on the woman's concern about being a criminal? Maybe focus on the feeling of remembering something you know you didn't do?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, and after looking over the draft you put on #thecritters, I think you are focusing too much on the object. Try to expand more on the Central Narrative.</p>
<p>Feel free to contact a member of the <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a> to get more crit, or PM me to take another look.</p>
<hr />
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Here, have a placeholder for a follow-up. I'll crit this within 12 hours.</span></p>
<p>I was summoned back by a PM. Let's crit this.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Here,&nbsp;have&nbsp;some&nbsp;more&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;OK,&nbsp;now&nbsp;give&nbsp;me&nbsp;back&nbsp;my&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>When no saliva enters the liquid and another person drinks it, the second drinker has a one-minute nosebleed and is presumed to have permanent retrograde amnesia.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>When someone drinks something, that person's saliva gets in the drink, so you probably can get rid of this part.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>[&#8230;] the anomaly, which was found on the sidewalk on which the woman slept.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm not entirely sure about this part. No one took the cup while all of this was happening? Not even another homeless person, or even a dog? Maybe you could write that the woman was sleeping somewhere hidden, like an abandoned building or something?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Through interviews with the woman, some aspects of the nature of the anomaly was accurately evaluated by SPC researchers before testing.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why did the Shark Punching Center get involved?</p>
<p>Also, are you planning to include a Testing Log? You can explain how the anomaly works through it, so the reader gets more familiar with the cup before reading the interviews.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The cup embodies this fear.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>While certainly the anomaly has something to do with the woman's story, it doesn't &quot;embodies&quot; the fear of being falsely accused. Maybe you can make the cup to only affect &quot;amoral&quot; memories? And maybe that's why the woman got the memory of a robbery? That way it can actually &quot;falsely accuse&quot; everyone who drinks from it.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, I think this has some potential, as it can be a good emotional article.</p>
<p>Feel free to contact a member of the <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a> to get more crit, or PM me to take another look.</p>
<p>(I highly recommend reaching out to other people, because I can't hand out greenlights yet.)</p>

