<p>I would suggest you don't use an existing SCP for this btw; it really limits what you can do narratively and lends itself to you writing something that forces a reader to read the other SCP to get yours, and generally you don't want readers to get distracted mid way through your writing in case they don't come back (also, since this is your first SCP, linking to a much better thing is likely to highlight how you aren't as good a writer; and like, it's fine to not be perfect but you don't necessarily want to draw attention to it, y'know?)</p>

